B. Important fee-collection architecture gate
The current Testnet /withdraw flow pays the recipient from ALBUKHR's Testnet payout wallet. It does not currently take a separate fee payment from the user's Pi wallet before paying the recipient. SQL-side arithmetic cannot honestly say the initiator paid the fee if there is no verified user-funded payment or explicit user-owned spendable balance.
Recommended flow when the fee is non-zero:
The client requests a server-generated withdrawal quote and sees recipient amount, fee, and total the initiator must pay.
The backend creates a withdrawal request and a unique fee assessment tied to that request.
The client pays the exact fee through the Pi SDK User-to-App payment flow.
The backend validates the payment ID, user identity, exact amount, metadata/withdrawal reference, Testnet environment, and successful server-side completion. A browser callback alone is not proof of payment.
Only after the fee payment is confirmed does the backend initiate the App-to-User payout for the full requested amount.
The payout is reconciled by the existing deterministic memo/transaction mechanism.
The fee is credited to the platform fee ledger only after confirmed fee payment. Project reward/principal reserves are debited only for the payout amount owed to the recipient, not for the user's fee.
If fee is zero, skip the fee-payment step and continue through the same idempotent payout/reconciliation path. If fee payment is pending/failed/cancelled, do not issue the payout. If payout fails after fee payment was confirmed, keep the request in a recoverable pending state and reconcile/retry; do not collect a second fee. Refund/reversal behavior for a permanently abandoned payout needs a recorded policy and auditable payment path.
For owner capital withdrawals, make the fee-payment step happen after ALBUKHR has approved the owner request and before payout, so an owner is not charged for a request that is rejected. Never let fee payment replace stage evidence, independent review, or the post-release coverage check.
C. SQL migration phases
Phase 0 — freeze and confirm baseline
Save a schema/function snapshot for the Testnet project.
Confirm current migration head and record current RLS/grants.
Keep project wallet configuration and verified liquidity unchanged.
Do not alter historical stakes or payment state.
The SQL draft in this ZIP is additive and inactive; it is not the full migration.
Phase 1 — additive schema
Use 03_DRAFT_ADDITIVE_SCHEMA.sql as a review draft for:
A singleton Testnet policy row containing the global liquidity floor, durations, tier-fee parameters, minimum withdrawal, and daily timezone. Policy is seeded inactive.
A shared fee-assessment table storing initiator, source withdrawal, per-user Lagos day, small-withdrawal ordinal, amount, fee, total sender debit, full recipient amount, policy version, fee payment reference/status, payout txid, and idempotency.
A platform-level fee ledger recording confirmed fee revenue/refunds without assigning the fee to a project's reward reserve.
RLS enabled and no direct anon/authenticated access to these new tables. Only trusted service-role/backend flows should read/write them.
This schema draft intentionally does not replace existing RPCs. Do not apply it alone and assume the feature is implemented.
Phase 2 — atomic database RPC integration
Patch and test these existing functions in a follow-up migration:
create_testnet_withdrawal: enforce 0.50 PI minimum for both reward and principal; enforce maturity lock for principal; use server-side fee policy; create an idempotent fee assessment; reserve only the reward/principal amount owed to the recipient; do not deduct the fee from project reserves.
complete_testnet_withdrawal_and_ledger: require fee assessment to be paid or not-required; debit project reserves by requested amount only; record the user-paid fee in the platform-level fee ledger only after the fee payment is reconciled; remain idempotent.
create_testnet_project_owner_withdrawal: remove percentage/net = requested - fee interpretation; recipient amount remains the requested amount; require the owner fee assessment/payment path before payout; preserve owner identity/project approval checks.
complete_testnet_project_owner_withdrawal: require approved state, verified fee status when applicable, and final payout txid; record the recipient payout at the full requested amount and record platform fee separately.
get_testnet_staking_coverage: implement the approved dynamic formula and ensure immediate rewards are 100% funded before stake confirmation. Keep stage/risk reserve percentages configurable and approved, not hardcoded.
create_testnet_stake_intent / finalize_testnet_stake_intent: ensure the allowed-duration check is on the server side and full reward reserve is confirmed before finalizing the commitment.
update_testnet_project_staking_offer: allow only the six configured durations; keep accepted stake terms immutable.
Add/adjust idempotency constraints and audit fields before exposing new endpoints.
Every SECURITY DEFINER function must use a fixed safe search_path, explicit authorization, and narrowly limited EXECUTE grants. Preserve RLS. Do not add public direct treasury-write policies.
